On Jan 30, 12:34 am, Jason Cannon <jasonca...@gmail.com> wrote:
> I suppose it's time to start smokey potions and fountains
> in search of wishes?

If you're high-level enough to be worrying about candles, you can
probably handle most anything a fountain can throw at you.  Do be sure
to use a one-handed weapon (unless you prefer to go without) and no
shield, and have a means of uncursing your equipment when you're all
done.  Start at the low-number dungeon levels first.

If smoky potions are majorly beneficial (extra healing, full healing,
gain anything), they should definitely all be blessed and quaffed,
just on principle.

If smoky potions are mildly beneficial (healing, speed, enlightenment,
see invisible) or harmless (fruit juice, restore ability, monster or
object detection) or harmless when blessed (booze, levitation) or
close enough to harmless as makes no difference for a high-level
character (oil, acid, sickness), or if you have the means to deal
easily with their detrimental effect (e.g., sleep resistance or a
unicorn horn), you can give serious thought to blessing and quaffing
as large a stack of them as you can readily obtain, especially if you
particularly need a wish.

If smoky potions are paralysis, don't mess with them unless you can
find a one-tile closet to lock yourself into, with a strong pet
outside the door and no keys on the level except the ones you're
carrying.  Potions of sleeping should only be attempted if you have
the resistance, hallucination only if you have a unicorn horn, and if
you do acid or sickness keep an eye on your hitpoints.

Potions of polymorph should probably not be quaffed in most cases.
Even if you have a ring of polymorph control, read the wiki article on
polyself thoroughly before attempting it.

If all of the above means you want to quaff smoky potions, but you
don't have very many of them, definitely have a look through the
alchemy article on the wiki to see if you can perhaps mix up some
more.  Some potions are much easier to obtain this way than others.
Also, if potions of object detection are smoky and you have more magic
marker charges than you need, consider repeatedly reverse-genociding
nymphs.

If you do get a wish, the wiki article on wishing claims that candles
are a special case when it comes to wishing for a certain number of
something, so you may be able to get all you need with just one wish.

> Or is there a better/safer way to obtain more candles?

I don't know if it's better or safer, but if you have a large surplus
of wands or scrolls of create monster you could try to get candles (or
sources of polypile) via death drops.  Cursing the scrolls yields a
larger supply of monsters.  If you are seriously high-level and can
manage to find a titan, you can avoid killing it (ideally, avoid
getting within melee range of it at all) and let it summon an endless
supply of monsters.  Candles and/or wands of polypile will get dropped
eventually, and possibly smoky potions as well, among other things.


